cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying article."
title: "embsurrogate: a deterministic, archivable surrogate of a text-embedding model"
abstract: >-
  embsurrogate reconstructs the text-to-vector map of a sentence-embedding model
  from input/output pairs alone and freezes it into a single file whose inference
  path depends on numpy only. Features are character 3-4-grams hashed with
  SHA-256 into 2^18 buckets with sublinear tf-idf weights and L2 normalisation;
  the estimator is kernel ridge regression in dual form with a tricube-weighted
  correction of residuals whose neighbourhood is searched in the output space
  after the first-stage prediction. The package targets the archival case: when
  the teacher model version disappears, vectors for new texts can still be
  computed deterministically from the frozen file. Measured fidelity on a fresh
  test set of 1200 texts with 43093 training pairs: Spearman rho of pairwise
  similarities 0.8075, median cosine to the teacher vector 0.8121, R-squared
  0.5348, recall@10 0.4402.
